# L §3.2: "A num that is an integer is accepted where an int is expected ... Any other num there is refused at
# that key (RUN-NOT-INT)."  6 / 3 = 2 (an integer num); 7 / 2 = 3.5 is not an integer.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
unit hour "godzina"

index ks = [a, b]
input x[k in ks]: int
input y: int

def c[k in ks]: int at reader
  rule base = x[k] / y

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  x[a] = 6
  x[b] = 7
  y = 3

ask q1: c[k] for k in ks law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1 (k = a): 2
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
q1 (k = b): refused: RUN-NOT-INT ...
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
